{
  "version": "v0.6",
  "grouping": "1:100k parent sheet",
  "rationale": "Adjacent 1:25k quadrants of the same 1:50k sheet share terrain, survey campaign, print run and scan batch, so splitting on the 1:25k sheet id is a weaker separation than the ids suggest. K-35-51-B-g and the annotated K-35-51-B-a are exactly that pair. Grouping on the 1:100k parent costs nothing and removes the doubt.",
  "test_note": "The test group is the four blind-annotated frozen sheets plus K-35-39-A-g, which shares the parent K-35-39 with two of them. K-35-39-A-g is not annotated and contributes no evaluation instances; it is held out rather than trained on, because training on a sheet that shares a parent with two blind test sheets is the leak this grouping exists to prevent.",
